-- title:
--   Level automorphisms act transitively on the supersingular chart fibre
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$ and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$.
--
--   **Reduction data at $q$.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in `A.nonunits`. $W$ is a finite set of places of the field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ (this field being generated over `ResidueField A` by the two Laurent series `jqModC` and `jqNModC … M'`), and the hypothesis `hW` says that membership in $W$ is equivalent to membership in `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: a place $w$ lies in $W$ exactly when $w$ is rational (the structure map of the base field onto the residue field of $w$ is surjective), satisfies the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and has $w$-value of `jGeomGen` lying in `ssJSet q`. The hypothesis `hle` asserts that the base change `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` of the level-$M'$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` (the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the series $j(q^{d})$ for $d \mid M'$) is contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`. Next, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with values in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` relative to $A$: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the former, a surjective residue homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto the latter with kernel the maximal ideal of `R₀.integers`, and a map `R₀.placeMap` on places, subject to the structure's axioms (the subring meets the constants in exactly $A$, residues of constants are the residues taken in $A$, every nonzero function has a nonzero-residue constant multiple, `placeMap` preserves degrees, and divisors of functions with nonzero residue push forward to divisors of their residues). The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image under `coeffMap A.subtype` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction `coeffMap (IsLocalRing.residue ↥A) y`. Finally $s$ is an element of $W$, i.e. one of these supersingular places.
--
--   **The small field $k_0$.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element lying in $A$; write $A_0 =$ `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` for the induced valuation subring of $k_0$. The hypotheses on $A_0$ are: `hdvr`, that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; `hunif`, that its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$; `hhens`, that $A_0$ is a henselian local ring; `hres`, that its residue field is algebraically closed. The hypothesis `hκ` requires that every element $a \in A$ is congruent to an element of $k_0 \cap A$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   **The auxiliary prime and the level field.** $\ell'$ is a prime with $\ell' \ne q$, $3 \le \ell'$ and $\ell' \nmid M'$; $\xi \in k_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity (`hξ`), and `hιξ` provides a ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$. $K$ is an intermediate field of $k_0((q))/k_0$, and `hK` identifies it with `laurentBaseChange ↥k₀ (xHFunctionField ((q * ℓ') ^ 2 * M') (levelH (q * ℓ') M'))`, where `levelH (q * ℓ') M'` is the kernel of the reduction map of unit groups $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell')^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell')^\times$. An algebra structure of $A_0$ on $K$ compatible with $k_0$ is assumed. Further, $j \in K$ is an element whose underlying Laurent series is `coeffEmb ↥k₀ jq`, the $j$-expansion with coefficients pushed into $k_0$, and $j \ne 0$.
--
--   Write $C =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin ↥A₀ ↥K j`, the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over `Algebra.adjoin ↥A₀ {j}`.
--
--   **The two maximal ideals.** $y$ and $y'$ are ideals of $C$, both maximal (`hy`, `hy'`), and both contain the image of $\pi_0$ under the structure map $A_0 \to C$ (`hπy`, `hπy'`).
--
--   **The two lying-over hypotheses.** `hover` and `hover'` are identical in shape, the first concerning $y$ and the second $y'$. Each requires the following for every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ belonging to `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, subject to: its image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` under `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` lies in `R₀.integers`; for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the base-changed $j$-expansion implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the base-changed $g$ (so $g$ has poles only where $j$ does); and the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$. Under these conditions, assuming that `qExpand ↥k₀ ℓ' (coeffEmb ↥k₀ g)` — the series $g$ read in $q^{\ell'}$ — lies in $K$ and that the resulting element of $K$ lies in $C$, then for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in `ResidueField A` equals `s.evalAt` of the $R_0$-residue of $g$ (the value at $s$ of the reduced function, pulled back through the rationality of $s$), the difference of that element of $C$ and the image of $c$ under $A_0 \to C$ lies in $y$ (respectively $y'$).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and a $k_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$, such that the following three assertions hold.
--
--   First, `IsLevelAutAt ↥k₀ (q * ℓ') ξ (q * ℓ') ((q * ℓ') ^ 2 * M') (levelH (q * ℓ') M') γ⁻¹ K τ`: for every weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$, every pair of modular forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ for the group [`CohCarrier.GammaH ((q * ℓ') ^ 2 * M') (levelH (q * ℓ') M')`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) viewed inside $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, every pair of integral power series $p_f, p_g$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose images in $\mathbb{C}[[q]]$ are the $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$ at width $1$, with the Laurent series attached to $p_g$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ nonzero, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is `coeffEmb ↥k₀` of the quotient of the Laurent series attached to $p_f$ and $p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$, one has
--   $$\iota_*\bigl(\tau x\bigr) \cdot \bigl(g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1}\bigr)^{\wedge} = \bigl(f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1}\bigr)^{\wedge},$$
--   where $\iota_*$ is coefficientwise application of $\iota$, $(\cdot)^{\wedge}$ denotes the $q$-expansion at width $1$ read as a Laurent series over $\mathbb{C}$, and `conjElemN m γ⁻¹` is the determinant-one real matrix $\begin{pmatrix} a & b/m \\ mc & d\end{pmatrix}$ formed from the entries of $\gamma^{-1}$ with $m = q\ell'$.
--
--   Second, $\tau$ maps $C$ into itself: every $f \in C$ has $\tau f \in C$.
--
--   Third, for every $f \in C$ with $\tau f \in C$, one has $f \in y$ if and only if $\tau f \in y'$; that is, $\tau$ carries $y$ to $y'$.
--
--   This is the transitivity step for the fibre of the integral chart of the level-$q\ell'$ modular curve above a supersingular place $s$ of the level-$M'$ curve in characteristic $q$: any two maximal ideals of the chart algebra $C$ that contain the uniformiser and reduce in the same way to the value of each integral level-$M'$ function at $s$ are interchanged by a level automorphism attached to an element of $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$. It feeds the construction of the supersingular fibre data for the level-$q\ell'$ curve, the computation of inertia at the supersingular points, and the counting of maximal ideals above $s$ in terms of the order of the level automorphism group and of the stabiliser.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_isLevelAutAt_map_chartAlgFin_eq_of_over_of_over_of_not_dvd.lean

